    "answer": {
      "short": "$f$ is even.\n\nSubstitution and $|-u|=|u|$ give $f(-x)=|x-1|+|x+1|=f(x)$ for every real $x$.",
      "worked": "Using $|-u|=|u|$,\n$$\\begin{align*}\nf(-x)&=|-x+1|+|-x-1|\\\\\nf(-x)&=|x-1|+|x+1|\\\\\nf(-x)&=f(x).\n\\end{align*}$$\nThus $f(-x)=f(x)$ for every real $x$, so $f$ is even.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 36
